<section class="reference-section" id="ganesha-birth"><div class="reference-section-heading"><h2>The Birth of Ganesha</h2><a href="/ganesha-birth.html">Return to story</a></div><div class="reference-content">
<p><strong>Shiva Mahapurana · Rudra Samhita · Kumara Khanda · chapters 13–18.</strong> This original condensed retelling was checked against the owner-supplied Gita Press Sanskrit–Hindi edition. The private PDF is not copied into the public website or repository.</p>
<p><strong>Shiva Mahapurana, Part I · Gita Press, Gorakhpur.</strong> Supplied scan PDF pages 798–824; printed pages 788–814. Chapter 13 begins the Shvetakalpa account of Ganesha’s birth, and chapter 18 concludes his appointment and the household’s reconciliation.</p>
<details><summary>Passages behind the key moments<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><ul><li><strong>Parvati’s wish, creation and appointment of her son:</strong> chapter 13, especially verses 10–33.</li><li><strong>The doorway dispute and conflict with Shiva’s ganas:</strong> chapters 14–15.</li><li><strong>The final combat and beheading:</strong> chapter 16.</li><li><strong>Parvati’s powers, her conditions, the northern search, elephant head and restoration:</strong> chapter 17.</li><li><strong>First worship, leader of the ganas, remover of obstacles and reconciliation:</strong> chapter 18, especially verses 1–39 and 61–74. The intervening verses expand vrata practice.</li></ul></details>
<p>The story is paraphrased rather than translated. Long combat passages, repeated speeches and the detailed vrata instructions are condensed. The reflection about boundaries and recognition is editorial, not a translated verse. No later Ganesha birth account is blended into this Kumara Khanda sequence.</p>
<p>The four reader illustrations and separate collection card are newly generated devotional interpretations. The early scenes correctly retain the child’s human head; the restoration scene shows the elephant-headed form without depicting severed remains or graphic violence.</p>
</div></section>
